Important addition to the reinterpret_cast bit:
Yes, you can technically do
foo* f = get_some_foo_ptr();
void* vp = f;
bar* b = static_cast<bar*>(vp);
This will interpret the exact address of the object stored in f as an object of type bar. Do not do this unless you are 100% sure of what you are doing, because odds are trying to read the object of type foo as though it had type bar will lead to problems.

